19:15 ; Psa 146:6 ; 1Chr 21:16 ; 29:11 ; 2Chr 2:11 +; as permanent Eccl 1:4 ; built on foundations, or pillars 1Sam 2:8 ; Psa 104:5 ; Job 38:4 ; Isa 48:13 ; 51:13 , 16 compare also 24:18 ; Psa 82:5 ; firm, so that its shaking is something terrible, & token of terrible power 1Sam 14:4 ; 2Sam 22:8 = Psa 18:8 ; Job 9:6 compare Psa 46:2 & 46:6 ; so also Amos 8:8 ; Isa 2:19 , 21 ; 24:18-19 , 20 ; Psa 60:4 ; 77:19 ; 99:1 ; 114:7 ; as hung on nothing Job 26:7 ; with waters under it Exod 20:4 = Deut 5:8 compare Gen 7:11 ; personified, especially as addressed, called to witness, etc. Deut 32:1 ; Jer 6:19 ; 22:29 ; Isa 1:2 ; Micah 1:2 ; Job 16:18 . c. earth = inhabitants of earth Gen 6:11 ; 1Kin 2:2 ; 10:24 ; Psa 33:8 ; 66:4 +? א ׳תֵּבֵל Prov 8:31 ; Job 37:12 . 2 land = a. country, territory, ׳א שִׁנְעָר Gen 10:10 , ׳א מִצְרַיִם 21:21 ; compare also 10:11 ; 11:28 , 31 ; 13:10 ; 47:6 , 27 ; 50:8 ; Isa 7:18 ; 23:1 ; 23:13 ; 27:13 ; Psa 78:12 ; Jer 25:20 ; 1Chr 1:43 ; personified Isa 62:4 ; Eccl 10:16-17 ,. b. district, region Gen 19:28 ; 22:2 ; Josh 11:3 ; Psa 42:7 . c. tribal territory Deut 34:2 ; Judg 21:21 ; 1Sam 9:4 , 16 ; 13:7 ; 1Kin 15:20 ; Isaiah 8:23; and still smaller territories 1Sam 9:4-5 ,. d. piece of ground Gen 23:15 . e. specifically land of Canaan, or Israel Gen 11:31 ; 12:1 ; 12:5 ; 12:6 ; 12:7 ; 31:3 ; Exodus 14:34; Deut 17:14 ; 18:9 ; 2Kin 5:2 , 4 +; especially object of יָרַשׁ possess Deut 3:20 +? Deuteronomy, Psalms and elsewhere; so after נָחַל Josh 19:49 +; נָתַן Deut 1:21 +. f. = inhabitants land Lev 19:29 ; Ezek 14:13 +? Deut 24:4 ; Zech 12:12 etc. g. used even of Sh®°ôl Job 10:21-22 , (compare Assyrian irƒit la târat , land without return , in Descent of Ishtar, see Jr 10. 65 ); see also Psa 139:15 ; Isa 44:23 . 3. a. ground , surface of ground = אֲדָמָה q. v. Gen 1:26 , 30 ; 18:2 ; 33:3 ; 38:9 ; Exod 4:3 ; 16:4 ; Ruth 2:10 ; 1Sam 5:4 + very often in Samuel. b. soil , as productive = אֲדָמָה Gen 1:11-12 , Lev 19:9 ; 25:9 ; 26:4 compare Num 14:7-8 , Isa 36:7 = 2Kin 18:32 ; Psa 72:6 ; 72:16 ; 107:34 ; 107:35 ; Ezra 9:12 ; Neh 9:35 . 4 אֶרֶץ in phrases: a. people of the land ׳עַםהָֿא of non-Israelites Gen 23:7 , 12 , 13 (P) Num 14:9 (JE); as well as Israel Lev 20:4 (H) 2Kin 15:5 ; 16:15 ; 21:24 (twice in verse); especially common people, opposed to officials, princes Lev 4:27 (P) Ezek 7:27 ; 2Kin 11:18-19 ,. b. in measurements of distance , הָא ׳כִּבְרַת the space or distance of country (see כּברה ) Gen 35:16 , so א ׳כִּבְרַת some distance 48:7 ; 2Kin 5:19 . c. הַמִּישׁוֺר אֶרֶץ the country of the plain, level or plain country Deut 4:33 ; Jer 48:21 ; ׳א מִישׁוֺר figurative Psa 143:10 (but read ᵑ6 אֹרַח Bi Gr Che, compare 27:11 ). d. ׳א חַיִּים land of the living Psa 27:13 ; ׳א הַחַיִּים 142:6 . e. הָא ׳קְצֵה end(s) of the earth Isa 42:10 ; 43:6 (|| רָחוֺק ) Psa 135:7 ; Prov 17:24 , so א ׳אַפְסֵי 30:4 +; הָא ׳קְצוֺת Isa 40:28 ; 41:5 , 9 . 5 plural אֲרָצוֺת is almost wholly late, Jer 16:15 6 t. Jeremiah; 23t. Ezekiel; Isa 36:20 ; 37:11 = 2Kin 18:35 ; 19:11 ( Isa 37:18 read הַגּוֺיִם see Che Di & compare 2Kin 19:17 ); 22t. Chronicles; Dan 9:7 ; 11:40 , 42 ; Psa 105:44 ; 106:27 ; 107:3 ; 116:9 ; besides these only P Gen 10:5 , 20 , 31 ; Lev 26:36 , 39 , except Gen 26:3-4 , (J R ) 41:54 (JE); it denotes lands, countries , often in contrast to Canaan, lands of the nations , etc., see especially absolute Ezek 20:32 ; 22:4 ; = the various petty divisions of Canaan afterward united under Israel's control Gen 26:3-4 , compare 1Chr 13:2 יִשְׂרָאֵל אַרְצוֺת , 2Chr 11:23 יְהוּדָה אַרְצוֺת .","rootNote":"from an unused root probably meaning to be firm ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 10","keyReferences":["1Chr 1 10","1Chr 1 19","1Chr 1 43","1Chr 1 45","1Chr 2 22","1Chr 4 40","1Chr 5 9","1Chr 5 11"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":2505,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 1 10","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":10,"